<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Chicken Plucker shipped one CPMods_Bases.xml across all of his mods, holding nine abstract
    bases - apparel, meals, weapons, workbenches - of which Retro Joy uses exactly two. The
    other seven are dropped here, and the two survivors are renamed.

    The renaming is for legibility only, and it is worth saying why it is NOT a fix. Eight
    subscribed mods ship that same file with the same nine names, which looks like a clash and
    is not one: XmlInheritance keeps nodesByName as a Dictionary<string, List<node>>, each node
    carrying the ModContentPack it came from, and GetBestParentFor picks among the homonyms the
    one belonging to the nearest mod in load order. Every mod therefore resolves to its own
    copy. Homonyms across mods are a supported arrangement, not an error.

    So the reason these two are renamed is that a file called RetroJoy_Bases.xml holding two
    bases named after somebody else's mods reads badly. Names of abstract defs never reach a
    save, so it costs nothing.

    Dropping the seven also removes the mod's only two dead fields: CPBenchBase carried
    <workSpeedPenaltyOutdoors> and <workSpeedPenaltyTemperature>, which BuildingProperties no
    longer has in 1.6. Nothing in Retro Joy inherited from it.
  -->

  <ThingDef Name="RetroJoy_BuildingBase" Abstract="True">
    <category>Building</category>
    <thingClass>Building</thingClass>
    <soundImpactDefault>BulletImpact_Metal</soundImpactDefault>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <drawerType>MapMeshAndRealTime</drawerType>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Light</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <repairEffect>Repair</repairEffect>
    <leaveResourcesWhenKilled>true</leaveResourcesWhenKilled>
    <filthLeaving>Filth_RubbleBuilding</filthLeaving>
    <statBases>
      <SellPriceFactor>0.70</SellPriceFactor>
    </statBases>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef Name="RetroJoy_FurnitureBase" ParentName="RetroJoy_BuildingBase" Abstract="True">
    <designationCategory>Furniture</designationCategory>
    <minifiedDef>MinifiedThing</minifiedDef>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>Furniture</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
